{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791242963,"nonce":"RRkVSTXD9R1fiKmpAgoTq3/t3B4=","title":"Canvas2D idles at about 300 MB against 169 MB for Interactions","message":"Measured 2026-10-05 with footprint -p, both idle after their first frame, Ash hybrid, M-series Mac. Interactions: 169 MB, of which 126 MB native MALLOC_SMALL and 11 MB VM_ALLOCATE (GC heap). Canvas2D: about 300-350 MB: MALLOC_SMALL 166 MB (+40), VM_ALLOCATE 41 MB (+30), owned unmapped graphics 41 MB, IOSurface 25 MB, MALLOC_LARGE 21 MB (Interactions has none). The GPU part is the window surface, the toolbar's backdrop-blur layers and the canvas data texture. Not yet broken down: which native allocations make the extra MALLOC_SMALL and MALLOC_LARGE (MallocStackLogging and malloc_history would show it), and whether the canvas data texture is sized larger than it needs.","files":null}]}